# Append to the .gitignore of the repository being documented.
#
# The durable artifacts are committed. A registry_hash match skips module
# analysis, which presumes the registry and the API snapshot are already on
# disk, and the grounding check reads api-surface.json on every run. Under CI
# caching a cold cache produces a matching hash with nothing behind it.
#
# The module summaries, the dependency pairs and the synthesis join them,
# because the foundation documents are written from those rather than from a
# symbol list. A rewrite after a code change then costs one call per changed
# module plus the synthesis, rather than a call per module in the repository.
# A stale summary is a cache miss the registry hash detects. None of these is
# rendered for a reader, which is why they are JSON: nobody browses them, so a
# stale one is a cache entry rather than a sentence somebody believes.
#
# Each run writes into `.docs-gen/<run>/`, so the durable artifacts are one
# level deeper than the root. The downloaded Vale packages sit in the root
# itself and are never committed.
.docs-gen/*
!.docs-gen/*/
.docs-gen/*/*
!.docs-gen/*/registry.json
!.docs-gen/*/api/
!.docs-gen/*/api-surface.json
!.docs-gen/*/modules/
!.docs-gen/*/dep-pairs.json
!.docs-gen/*/onboarding.json
.docs-gen/vale-packages/
